      { q: "Why were the Middle colonies nicknamed 'the breadbasket colonies'?", choices: ["They imported all their food", "They only grew bread, not wheat", "Their fertile land produced abundant grain, especially wheat", "They had no farming at all"], answer: 2, explain: "Fertile land made the Middle colonies productive grain farmers, especially of wheat." },
      { q: "What made Pennsylvania notably different from many other colonies?", choices: ["It banned all immigration", "It had no government at all", "It was known for religious tolerance, founded by Quaker William Penn", "It was the smallest colony by far"], answer: 2, explain: "Pennsylvania was known for religious tolerance under founder William Penn." },
      { q: "What labor system did the Southern colonies' plantation economy become deeply dependent on?", choices: ["Robotic labor", "No labor was needed", "Enslaved African labor", "Only paid free labor"], answer: 2, explain: "The Southern plantation economy became deeply dependent on enslaved labor." },
      { q: "Was colonial society across all three regions generally equal for everyone?", choices: ["Equality wasn't a concept yet", "Yes, everyone had exactly equal rights", "Only in the Southern colonies was it equal", "No, it was strictly hierarchical, with wealthy landowners holding disproportionate power"], answer: 3, explain: "Colonial society was strictly hierarchical, far from equal for all." }
