      { q: "What caused a painful split within the suffrage movement over the 15th Amendment?", choices: ["The amendment granted voting rights by race but not gender, dividing suffragists on how to respond", "The amendment had nothing to do with voting rights", "The amendment granted women the vote immediately", "All suffragists agreed completely on every issue"], answer: 0, explain: "The 15th Amendment's race-based (not gender-based) voting rights divided suffragists." },
      { q: "What tactics did Alice Paul and the National Woman's Party use to intensify the movement?", choices: ["Violent armed rebellion", "Complete withdrawal from all public activity", "Dramatic public demonstrations and 'Silent Sentinel' picketing of the White House", "Only private letter-writing campaigns"], answer: 2, explain: "Paul's group used dramatic public demonstrations and White House picketing." },
      { q: "What role did World War I play in the suffrage movement's eventual success?", choices: ["Women's wartime workforce contributions strengthened the argument for suffrage as democratic fairness", "The war had no effect on the movement at all", "The war ended the suffrage movement completely", "The war delayed suffrage by several decades"], answer: 0, explain: "Women's WWI contributions strengthened suffrage arguments." },
      { q: "What significant issue remained unresolved even after the 19th Amendment's ratification in 1920?", choices: ["Many Black women continued facing discriminatory voter suppression tactics, especially in the South", "The amendment was immediately repealed", "Every woman in America could vote with no obstacles whatsoever", "Men lost their right to vote entirely"], answer: 0, explain: "Discriminatory voter suppression continued to affect Black women's actual voting access." }
